  "result": "The six-question quiz on O4 is ready in `quizzes/0002.json`, with its key in `keys/0002.json`. I wrote it before any lesson on O4, so it checks the objective itself and is ahead of the lessons. I wrote the items from what I already know about workflows and agents and did not search for a source. I answered each item from its stem alone to check that it has one defensible answer.\n\n- **Coverage:** The quiz has four multiple-choice items, one one-word short answer and one numeric item.\n- **Who owns the control flow (q1, q4):** q1 asks what separates an agent from a workflow. q4 gives code that always calls the same tool once and asks you to classify it.\n- **Choosing a fixed workflow (q2, q3, q5, q6):** These items use the makerspace assistant. They cover which task needs an agent, which design suits a fixed sequence, why a workflow costs less, and how many extra model calls an agent makes over a week.\n- **Misconception ids:** I used M7 to M10 for the wrong options, which are new ids. I used them for model size, \"workflows can't use tools\", \"workflows loop, agents don't\", and \"agents are always better\". They don't clash with M1, M3, M4 and M6 from quiz 0001, but check them against any ids you track elsewhere.\n\nWhen you're ready, you can take it in the chat or submit your answers as a file.",
